@SINIOUR If you're serious about knowing more about this, it's best to be less combative with your responses and spend a little more time looking at what information has already been released.

The idea was explained in a Copi Cafe awhile back saying it would cost X dollars to rent server space and they decided to allow the community members the opportunity to receive that money, in the form of a Copi reward as opposed to just cut a check to Amazon or Google to rent server space. 26 million was allocated for the first year of rewards (called a budget) after that the node function will be tuned to best suit the game operation in the hands of the operators and the rewards distribution will continue with the new budgeted Copi for rewards distribution. 

Unlike most every other crypto related thing out there, this one isn't a ponzi scheme. The more time you spend here the more you might come to realize this team is the real deal, looking to still be here in the next 10 years.
